# Security headers for chatterbox.fans, in Cloudflare Pages syntax.
#
# These have now lived in three places, and the reason is worth keeping: they
# started in web/public/_headers, which is this syntax, while the site was on
# Firebase Hosting — which does not read this file, so they shipped nowhere
# while looking in review exactly like a control. They were ported into
# firebase.json's `headers`, verified against the hosting emulator, and are
# ported back here now that the site is on Pages. firebase.json's hosting
# block is gone in the same commit, so there is again exactly one file that
# decides this.
#
# ## Why there is no `/*` rule for Permissions-Policy
#
# Firebase merged overlapping rules by *overriding* the header, so a `**` rule
# denying the camera and an `/app/**` rule allowing it left the app with the
# permissive value. Cloudflare does not override — "requests matching multiple
# rules inherit all applicable headers. Duplicate headers are joined with
# commas" — and Permissions-Policy resolves a repeated directive by taking the
# *first* occurrence. A `/*` rule with `microphone=()` would therefore win over
# `/app/*`'s `microphone=(self)` and the browser would refuse the microphone
# and camera for the whole web client: no calls, no voice messages, and nothing
# in the app able to explain why.
#
# So the three headers that are identical everywhere go on `/*`, and
# Permissions-Policy is written once per path group with no overlap between
# them. Any header added below has to be checked the same way: if two rules can
# match one request, they must not both set it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The marketing pages. Pages strips `.html`, so these are the served paths:
# `/` for English, `/index.zh-Hans` and `/privacy.zh-Hans` for the rest.
#
# default-src 'none' is enforced and can be, because these pages are generated
# and load nothing but their own stylesheet, icon and inline SVG.
/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

/index*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

/privacy*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

# The web client. microphone and camera are (self) because calls and voice
# messages need them; geolocation stays denied — live location is sent from the
# mobile app, and the web client has no feature that asks.
#
# The CSP here stays Report-Only. It has never been exercised against the
# running app, and an enforced policy that is wrong in one directive takes the
# whole client down rather than degrading. It becomes Content-Security-Policy
# once the reports from a real deployment come back clean.
/app
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(self), camera=(self), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.gstatic.com https://www.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://*.firebaseio.com wss://*.firebaseio.com https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://firebaseappcheck.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://fcm.googleapis.com https://*.cloudfunctions.net; frame-src https://www.google.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

/app/*
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(self), camera=(self), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.gstatic.com https://www.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://*.firebaseio.com wss://*.firebaseio.com https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://firebaseappcheck.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://fcm.googleapis.com https://*.cloudfunctions.net; frame-src https://www.google.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# Vite fingerprints these, so they can be cached forever.
/app/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
